RudeConfig NEWS - User visible changes.
See ChangeLog for more detailed information on internal changes
See the end for copying conditions.

_______________________________________________________________________________
Release 6.1.0 - Matthew Flood 2026-07-30

	- REMOVED: the autotools build (configure, configure.ac, Makefile.am,
	  Makefile.in, aclocal.m4, config.guess, config.sub, install-sh,
	  ltmain.sh, missing, depcomp and INSTALL).  It has been deprecated
	  since the CMake build landed, and the config.guess it shipped dated
	  from 2003, so it could not configure on any ARM machine - today that
	  means every Apple Silicon Mac and every ARM Linux server.  Its
	  install-sh was also committed without an executable bit, so
	  "make install" failed on macOS.  Check out v6.0.1 or earlier if you
	  still need it.
	- Consumers using FetchContent no longer inherit this project's demo
	  and test_* targets.  Tests and examples are now added only when this
	  is the top-level project.
	- The FetchContent example in README.md now pins GIT_TAG to v6.0.1
	  rather than tracking master.
	- The plain README no longer points at the removed INSTALL file or at
	  rudeserver.com addresses that stopped resolving years ago; bug
	  reports go to GitHub issues.

_______________________________________________________________________________
Release 6.0.1 - Matthew Flood 2026-07-30

	- An empty value is now written with its delimiter ("key = ") rather
	  than as a bare "key".  The bare form reloaded correctly through
	  this library, so it looked harmless, but other ini readers treat a
	  line with no delimiter as malformed or as a valueless flag - so an
	  empty string did not survive leaving rudeconfig.
	- deleteSection() now returns false when the section has already been
	  deleted, as documented.  It reported success every time it was
	  called for a section that still existed in the file, deleted or
	  not.
	- Asking about a section that does not exist no longer inserts an
	  empty entry into the internal section map.  setSection() and
	  deleteSection() looked names up with std::map::operator[], which
	  default-inserts, so repeatedly querying unknown section names grew
	  the map for the lifetime of the object.
	- load() now fails when given a directory.  A directory opens
	  successfully as an ifstream on POSIX and then reads as empty, so
	  load(".") returned true and handed back a silently empty
	  configuration with no error set.

_______________________________________________________________________________
Release 6.0.0 - Matthew Flood 2026-07-30

	- MAJOR VERSION BUMP: rude::Config is no longer copyable (see below).
	  That is a source-incompatible change, so this is 6.0.0 rather than
	  5.1.1.  The shared-library ABI is unchanged and the soname stays at
	  3; only code that copied a Config needs to change, and such code was
	  already double-freeing.
	- Fixed out-of-bounds read in getDataNameAt() and getDataValueAt().
	  Both indexed the data-member vector with no bounds check, so an
	  out-of-range index read unowned memory instead of returning NULL
	  as documented.  The sentinel loop recommended by config.h's own
	  example was therefore unsafe on every use.  They now return NULL.
	- rude::Config is no longer copyable.  It owns its implementation
	  through a raw pointer, so the compiler-generated copy left two
	  objects owning it and double-freed on destruction; putting a
	  Config in a container or passing it by value corrupted the heap.
	  Copy construction and copy assignment are now deleted, which turns
	  that silent corruption into a compile error.  Pass by reference.
	- Fixed pkg-config file: it hardcoded the prefix given at configure
	  time, so installing with "cmake --install --prefix <dir>" produced
	  a rudeconfig.pc still pointing at the configure-time prefix (by
	  default /usr/local).  The prefix is now relative to ${pcfiledir}.
	- Config::version() now reports the release version of the library
	  (for example "6.0.0").  It previously returned a hardcoded "3.0"
	  interface.implementation pair that had not tracked a release since
	  2005, so callers could not tell what they had linked.  The value is
	  now generated from the build so it cannot drift again.
	- Added regression tests for all of the above, including an
	  out-of-range enumeration test that fails under AddressSanitizer
	  without the fix, and a test that version() matches the build.

_______________________________________________________________________________
Release 5.1.0 - Matthew Flood 2026-07-30

	- Fixed infinite loop in Config::load() on platforms where char
	  is unsigned (Linux/ARM, Linux/PowerPC): the parser stored
	  istream::peek() results in char, so EOF was never detected.
	- New CMake build system (autotools files retained but deprecated);
	  installs CMake package config and pkg-config files.
	- Code modernized to compile cleanly as C++17 with -Wall -Wextra
	  (removed 'register', sprintf -> snprintf, UTF-8-safe isspace).
	- Added test suite (ctest) and GitHub Actions CI covering Linux
	  x86_64/ARM, macOS, and Windows, plus an ASan/UBSan job.
	- New README with verified quick-start example.

_______________________________________________________________________________
Release 5.0.5-1 - Matthew Flood 2007-02-01

	- Renamed header include guards in config.h from 
	  INCLUDED_CONFIG_H to INCLUDED_RUDE_CONFIG_H
	  The new guards are less generic and safer to use overall. 

